-- title:
--   End local ring 𝒪 lies in the exceptional valuation ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $5\le q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` requires a ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which, by `hK`, equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79): the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image, under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), of the $\mathbb Q$-rational $q$-expansion function field of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ and group $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, Henselian and with algebraically closed residue field, such that $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hξA`), together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero whose Laurent series is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular $j$-invariant (`hj`). Let $\varpi$ be a uniformiser, $\mathfrak m_A=(\varpi)$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t\in A$ a tame parameter: $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C:=$ `chartAlgFin A K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and let $y\subset C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) at which $j$ is supersingular: by `hss`, for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi\colon C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin}\ A\ K\ j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j$-invariants for which every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   Throughout, for $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ a *level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$* means an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29), that is: for every weight $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ on the group attached to $\Gamma_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, with the Laurent series of $p_g$ nonzero, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of $p_f/p_g$, and every embedding $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, the $\iota$-image of the Laurent series of $\tau x$, multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$, equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$.
--
--   Let $X:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two affine charts $\mathrm{Spec}\,C$ and $\mathrm{Spec}\,$`chartAlgFin A K j⁻¹` along the middle chart, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$. The hypothesis `hArig` (a Drinfeld-chart witness, seven clauses, summarised here) requires: for every point $z$ of $X$ such that the germ at $z$ of the global section coming from $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,z}$, and every point $y'$ of $\mathrm{Spec}\,C$ mapping to $z$ at which $j$ is supersingular in the above sense, there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma\colon A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f-(X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1)\in(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ onto $S:=W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v-f\,u)$, such that, writing $\mathrm{toC}$ for the completion map, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map and $\mathrm{germY}$ for the germ map $C\to\mathcal O_{X,z}$ at $y'$: (1) constants match, $e$ sending the germ of $a\in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (2) every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ maps $C$ into $C$; (3) if moreover $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$; (4) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and congruent to the identity modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ with $\theta$ intertwining the action of $\tau$ through $e\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$, $\theta$ fixing all constants, $\theta(X_j)\equiv\sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, $c^{q+1}\equiv1$, $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, $c\equiv1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, and $c\not\equiv1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (5) two primes of $S$ not containing both classes of $X_0,X_1$, containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$ and containing elements with linear parts $a_1X_0+b_1X_1$ and $a_2X_0+b_2X_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$ with $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions along $e\circ\mathrm{toC}$; (6) for a prime $P$ of $S$ of the same kind with linear part $X_0$, an element $a\in C$ has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)$ in the contraction of $P$ precisely when every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; (7) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0\in A$ with that element congruent to $a_0$ modulo $y'$, an integer $e_0\ge1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ form $\sum_{i\le e_0}(\text{coeff of }X_0^iX_1^{e_0-i}\text{ in }h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b\in W$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$, and with $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(j_{q\ell}-a_0)))$ equal to the class of $h$.
--
--   Fixed data of this kind are then given: a point $z$ of $X$ with the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ (`hϖz`) in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ (`hz`), a point $y'$ of $\mathrm{Spec}\,C$ with `ιFin`-image $z$ (`hy'`), supersingular in the above sense (`hss'`) and with $y'$ corresponding to $y$ (`hy'y`), and a particular witness $W_1,\sigma_1,f_1,u_1,v_1,e_1$ subject to `hσ₁`, `hu₁`, `hv₁`, `hf₁` and to `hW₁`, which asserts for this data exactly the seven clauses (1)–(7) listed above.
--
--   Next, $J$ is an ideal of $C$ which by `hJ` is the infimum of all ideals of the form $\tau^{-1}\bigl((e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY})^{-1}(\mathrm{span}\{\mathrm{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1\varpi_t),\mathrm{mkS}\,X_0,\mathrm{mkS}\,X_1\})\bigr)$, taken over $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$. The $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$ is, by `hB`, generated over $C$ by $\{x\in K\mid \exists\, i\in J,\ x\varpi_t=i\}$, i.e. $C[J/\varpi_t]$. Further, $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`), and four groups of hypotheses are imposed: `hR1` ($C\le B$, and every element of $K$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\neq0$); `hR2` ($A\to B$ formally smooth and of finite presentation, and $B/(\varpi)$ of Krull dimension at most $1$); `hR3` (five clauses: an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$; $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; for $b\in C$, $b\in y$ iff $b$ lies in $W$ and in $\mathfrak m_W$; and $f\in W$ iff $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h\notin\mathfrak m_W$); and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here: for each $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) whose kernel consists of the elements landing in $\mathfrak m_W$, compatible with $A\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, and equivariant for level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, preserving $W$, through an element $c\in\mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathtt{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ in the kernel [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) of $\det\cdot(\ )^{q+1}$ acting by [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325), with $c\neq1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, preserve $B$; every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ receives, under some level automorphism with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, the whole set of elements of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$; an element of $B$ sent into $\mathfrak m_W$ by all such automorphisms is divisible by $\varpi$; and a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, which preserves $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$).
--
--   Finally, `hjK` and `hjC` place [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) in $K$ and in $C$; $m\ge1$ satisfies $\varpi^m=\varpi_t\cdot(\text{unit})$ (`hmt`); and $\mathcal O$ is a subring of $K$ subject to the following end data. By `hO` there are $a\in J$, $a\neq0$, a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a:=C[J/a]$ (the $A$-subalgebra generated over $C$ by $\{x\in K\mid\exists\,i\in J,\ xa=i\}$) such that $\mathcal O$ is the set of quotients $g/h$ with $g,h\in B_a$, $h\notin P$, every element of $y$ is a non-unit in $\mathcal O$, and $B$ is not contained in $\mathcal O$. Moreover $\mathcal O$ is local (`hOloc`) and Noetherian (`hOnoe`), contains $C$ (`hCO`), and for $b\in C$ one has $b\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ iff $b\in y$ (`hOy`). There is a ring isomorphism $\iota_1$ from the $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$-adic completion of $\mathcal O$ onto `UVCrossingModel W₁ ((σ₁ ϖ)^m)` $=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-C((\sigma_1\varpi)^m))$, carrying the image of $a\in A$ to `UVCrossingModel.const` of $\sigma_1 a$ (`hι₁c`). Elements $a\in C$ with $a\in J$ and $a\neq0$, $c\in\mathcal O$ and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that quotient are given with: every $i\in J$ of the form $a\cdot o$ with $o\in\mathcal O$ (`hJa`); $a\,c=\varpi_t$ in $K$ (`hac`); $\iota_1$ of the image of $a$ equal to $\gamma_V\cdot$`UVCrossingModel.V ((σ₁ ϖ)^m)` (`hιa`); and $\iota_1$ of the image of $c$ equal to $\gamma_U\cdot$`UVCrossingModel.U ((σ₁ ϖ)^m)` (`hιc`). Lastly, `hyB` requires that the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of $y$ be prime.
--
--   Under all these hypotheses the conclusion is a single assertion: every $f\in K$ which lies in $\mathcal O$ lies in $W$; that is, $\mathcal O\subseteq W$ inside $K$.
--
--   This is the dominance step in the local analysis of the integral model of the modular curve at a supersingular point: after blowing up the weighted centre $J$, the local ring $\mathcal O$ attached to an end of the blow-up is shown to be contained in the exceptional valuation subring $W$ of $K$, whose residue data is governed by the Drinfeld coordinate ring. It feeds the construction of a ring homomorphism and completion isomorphism for ends of the blown-up chart in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_tangent_coords_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_tangent_coords_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked).
